# --- Global gitignore: machine facts, never project facts ---
#
# Git reads this file at $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git/ignore BY DEFAULT, with no
# core.excludesFile setting anywhere. Verified on git 2.43 with a zero
# config environment: check-ignore attributes the match to this file.
#
# THE RULE FOR WHAT BELONGS HERE: only things that are true of the
# MACHINE, never things that are true of any project. OS metadata and
# editor swap files exist because of where a repository is checked out,
# not because of what it contains, so ignoring them per repository means
# repeating the same lines in every .gitignore forever.
#
# Nothing project-shaped goes here, however tempting. A globally ignored
# node_modules or .env changes what git status reports in EVERY repository
# on the machine, including ones whose own .gitignore made a different
# choice, and it does so invisibly to anyone reading that repository.

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Windows
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor swap and backup droppings
*.swp
*.swo
*~
